# Redis Lua dual admit (AINav)

Canonical doc: `docs/REDIS_LUA_DUAL_ADMIT.md` · script: `scripts/redis/dual_consume.lua`

## Non-negotiables

- **Validate-all-then-write-all** — no HSET before every predicate passes
- **Same-slot keys** — `ainav:req:{request_id}`, `ainav:tok:{request_id}:…`
- **EVALSHA** + sticky SHA; on `NOSCRIPT` → `SCRIPT LOAD` once + retry once
- **Business denies** return `{err='…'}`; do not Lua `error()` for already_consumed / hash_mismatch
- **Hash + PDP in app**; Lua only compares short fields and burns
- **Fail-closed** — Redis errors / timeouts ≠ admit success; no SoR write without `ok`
- **Effect after ok** with idempotency key (DecisionRecord path)
- **Do not claim multi-host dual in product** until fixtures pass on Redis

## Script shape

```text
KEYS[1]=request, KEYS[2..N]=tokens
ARGV[1]=expected_hash, ARGV[2]=now
checks → return err OR burn all → return ok
```

## Ops

- Profile: `SLOWLOG` + client RTT histogram; target sub-ms script, one RTT
- Cluster: script cache is per node; load on slot owners
- Never `SCRIPT FLUSH` on live traffic; never policy-in-Lua; never log token secrets
